<h3 style=3D'tab-stops:.5in .75in 1.0in 1.25in 1.5in right 7.0in'>Robust Im=
age
Transmission</h3>

<p class=3DMsoNormal style=3D'margin-left:.5in;text-align:justify'><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times New Roman"'>Developed error detection and corre=
ction
methodology for corrupted DCT coefficients caused by transmission of DCT co=
ded
images over a noisy wireless channel. This method is based on the propertie=
s of
discrete cosine transforms and the transmission of exact values of a few
reference pixels.<span style=3D'mso-spacerun:yes'>&nbsp; </span>These allow=
 us to
identify the error pattern.<span style=3D'mso-spacerun:yes'>&nbsp; </span>K=
nowing
the error pattern it is possible to locate the corrupted DCT coefficients a=
nd
correct them. A journal paper based on this work has been submitted.<o:p></=
o:p></span></p>

<p class=3DMsoNormal style=3D'text-align:justify'><span style=3D'font-famil=
y:"Times New Roman"'><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></span></p>

<h3 style=3D'tab-stops:.5in .75in 1.0in 1.25in 1.5in right 7.0in'>Image Qua=
lity
Measure</h3>

<p class=3DMsoBodyTextIndent3 style=3D'margin-left:.5in;text-align:justify;
tab-stops:.5in 45.0pt .75in'>Developed objective image quality measures that
will resemble the human subjective image quality measure by taking into acc=
ount
the human visual characteristics. This measure can be used to evaluate imag=
es
that undergo transmission and error concealment. It is unique because it
provides both the percentage of the corrupted area of the image and the
signal-to-noise ratio. A journal paper is under preparation.</p>

<p class=3DMsoBodyTextIndent3 style=3D'margin-left:0in;text-align:justify;
tab-stops:.5in 45.0pt .75in'><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<h3 style=3D'tab-stops:.5in .75in 1.0in 1.25in 1.5in right 7.0in'>Error
Concealment</h3>

<p class=3DMsoNormal style=3D'margin-left:.5in;text-align:justify'><span
style=3D'font-family:"Times New Roman"'>Developed an algorithm to conceal
corrupted blocks in the image by using a few reference pixels in the block =
and
the uncorrupted adjacent blocks to estimate the pixels of the corrupted blo=
ck. <o:p></o:p></span></p>

<p class=3DMsoNormal><span style=3D'font-family:"Times New Roman"'><o:p>&nb=
